{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Unless she turned aside.</b> Had she not turned aside before Me when I killed her, I would have killed you and given her life. From this we learn that the she-ass died after she spoke — either by way of the Midrash, which says it was so the Amorites would not make an idol of her; or for the reason that she had already completed her designated purpose, as decreed during the six days of creation at twilight, in the manner we find with the fish of Jonah, where Scripture says (Jonah 2): ״וימן ה׳ דג גדול לבלוע את יונה״ — and the reason for גדול (״great״), though it was great in body, there were many fish in the sea greater than it; and the intent of the expression וימן is that it was designated for this from the six days of creation, which is why it says לבלוע (״to swallow״) and not ויבלע (״and it swallowed״). And once it swallowed him and fulfilled its designation, the fish died, for it was created only for that — and this is why Scripture afterward changes the expression from דג (masculine) to דגה (feminine), as it is written (ibid.): ״ויתפלל יונה אל ה׳ אלהיו ממעי הדגה״, and concerning this he said: ״מבטן שאול שועתי״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:18.944733990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}